{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **November 6, 2026**:\n\n- **Existing trust adding a new ETF series:** [Rule 485(a)(2)](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/17/230.485) normally provides **automatic effectiveness 75 calendar days after filing**, unless a later permissible date is designated or the SEC accelerates effectiveness. The usual **60-day** Rule 485(a) period applies to other amendments—not amendments adding a series.\n- **New trust’s initial registration:** This is not a post-effective amendment, so the 75-day rule does not apply. Securities Act Section 8(a) supplies a 20-day statutory baseline, but initial registrations ordinarily include delaying amendments pending SEC review and declared effectiveness.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Effectiveness is neither SEC approval nor a guaranteed trading date. Staff comments, further amendments or deferred effectiveness can extend registration; exchange listing, seed capital, authorized-participant arrangements and operational readiness must also be completed. No separate exemptive relief removes one potential dependency, not these others."}}
